 R←Test_API_024(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;home;expected;this
⍝ Runs "IdentifyObject": checks that every documented form of the argument resolves to the
⍝ very same filename, and that this filename is relative to the root of the project.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 home←##.CiderConfig.HOME
 expected←'APLSource/APLGit2/IdentifyObject.aplf'   ⍝ Note that this name is unique in this project
 this←'#.APLGit2'

 ⍝ An APL object, relative to the project space as well as fully qualified:
 →T.PassesIf expected≡⊃this G.IdentifyObject'APLGit2.IdentifyObject'
 →T.PassesIf expected≡⊃this G.IdentifyObject'#.APLGit2.APLGit2.IdentifyObject'

 ⍝ A filename, relative to the root of the project, with and without a leading "./":
 →T.PassesIf expected≡⊃this G.IdentifyObject expected
 →T.PassesIf expected≡⊃this G.IdentifyObject'./',expected

 ⍝ An absolute filename pointing into an opened project:
 →T.PassesIf expected≡⊃this G.IdentifyObject home,'/',expected

 ⍝ Just a filename: this must be found in the source folder of the project:
 →T.PassesIf expected≡⊃this G.IdentifyObject'IdentifyObject.aplf'

 ⍝ Backslashes must not make a difference:
 →T.PassesIf expected≡⊃this G.IdentifyObject'APLSource\APLGit2\IdentifyObject.aplf'

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
